{
 "artist": "Vincent van Gogh",
 "slug": "vincent-van-gogh",
 "born": 1853,
 "died": 1890,
 "nationality": "Dutch",
 "facts": [
  {
   "text": "Van Gogh signed only 133 of his 840 known paintings, about 15 per cent.",
   "source": "https://www.vangoghmuseum.nl/en/about/news-and-press/news/20260813-new-research-reveals-the-story-behind-van-goghs-vincent-signature",
   "source_name": "Van Gogh Museum"
  },
  {
   "text": "He almost always signed with his first name only; in March 1888 he wrote that his name should appear in catalogues as he signed it on the canvases, \"Vincent and not Vangogh\", because people in France could not pronounce it.",
   "source": "https://www.vangoghmuseum.nl/en/art-and-stories/vincent-van-gogh-faq/why-did-vincent-van-gogh-sign-his-paintings-with-vincent-and-not-his-surname",
   "source_name": "Van Gogh Museum"
  },
  {
   "text": "He signed no paintings before 1884, although he had started painting in oils in 1881; he signed drawings earlier.",
   "source": "https://www.vangoghmuseum.nl/en/about/news-and-press/news/20260813-new-research-reveals-the-story-behind-van-goghs-vincent-signature",
   "source_name": "Van Gogh Museum"
  },
  {
   "text": "He signed more often in Paris and soon after arriving in Arles; after entering the asylum at Saint-Rémy in 1889 he signed hardly any paintings, and in Auvers he signed only one, a portrait he gave to its sitter, Adeline Ravoux.",
   "source": "https://www.vangoghmuseum.nl/en/about/news-and-press/news/20260813-new-research-reveals-the-story-behind-van-goghs-vincent-signature",
   "source_name": "Van Gogh Museum"
  },
  {
   "text": "He often signed paintings he gave to family and friends, and usually left unsigned the copies he made after prints by Millet, Rembrandt and Delacroix.",
   "source": "https://www.vangoghmuseum.nl/en/about/news-and-press/news/20260813-new-research-reveals-the-story-behind-van-goghs-vincent-signature",
   "source_name": "Van Gogh Museum"
  },
  {
   "text": "On Seascape near Les Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer (1888) he wrote that he put \"a very outrageous red signature\" in the lower left \"because I wanted a red note in the green\".",
   "source": "https://www.vangoghmuseum.nl/en/about/news-and-press/news/20260813-new-research-reveals-the-story-behind-van-goghs-vincent-signature",
   "source_name": "Van Gogh Museum"
  }
 ],
